UPDATE companies SET description='Madison County Metalwork was founded in 2021 in Norfolk, Nebraska, by three local tradesmen—Josh Bailey, Ryan Showalter, and Brian Wolfe—who together brought more than 60 years of combined fabrication and machining experience. The partners formed the company to provide custom fabrication and machine work to the surrounding region, drawing on backgrounds that ranged from Army service and laser-department management to formal training in welding, tool-and-die, and collision repair.

While the facility size and headcount are not publicly disclosed, the founders’ expertise spans a multitude of materials and processes, allowing the company to handle projects from prototype through production runs for a variety of industrial sectors.

Customers come from medical, food-processing, rubber, steel, ethanol, and agricultural industries, reflecting the founders’ prior work in area job shops. The company serves regional manufacturers and OEMs that require precision metal components and fabricated assemblies.

The business was started with a mission to deliver precise, quality metalwork while excelling in its trade specialties and expanding its service offerings. The partners emphasize a hands-on, project-by-project approach, applying decades of practical knowledge to each job.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Precision machining", "Welding", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Grinding", "Heat treating", "Wire EDM", "Laser cutting"], "industries": ["Medical", "Food processing", "Rubber", "Steel", "Ethanol", "Agriculture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Laser cutting systems", "CNC milling machines", "CNC turning lathes", "Grinding machines", "Heat treating furnaces", "Wire EDM machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-custom machining and fabrication tailored to each project", "Over 60 years of combined trade experience among founders", "Precision and quality focus across welding, machining, and fabrication", "Regionally focused service for Nebraska and surrounding areas"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2021 -> /about", "Three founders: Josh Bailey, Ryan Showalter, Brian Wolfe -> /about", "Over 60 years combined experience -> /about", "Location: Norfolk, Nebraska -> db", "Custom fabrication and machining services -> /", "Processes: welding, milling, turning, grinding, heat treating, wire EDM, laser cutting -> /about", "Industries served: medical, food, rubber, steel, ethanol, agriculture -> /about", "Mission: precise and quality metalwork -> /about", "Josh Bailey: Army veteran, laser department management -> /about", "Ryan Showalter: welding and fabrication background -> /about", "Brian Wolfe: tool and die, machining background -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "provide fabrication and machine work to our region", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='madison-county-metalwork' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Magic Valley Equipment was established in 1985 in Paul, Idaho. The company operates as a dealership for agricultural equipment and parts, with a focus on sugar beet machinery. No founders are named in the available records, and ownership structure is not disclosed.

The business supplies equipment and parts for sugar beet, potato, hay, tillage, grain, and planting operations. As a shortline dealer, it maintains relationships with multiple vendors and distributors to source a broad range of products. The facility includes a full-service shop that handles repair and rebuild work for customer machinery.

Customers are primarily agricultural producers across the western United States, including sugar beet growers, potato farms, and operations focused on hay, grain, and tillage.

The company emphasizes its ability to locate hard-to-find items through its vendor network, stating that if a part is not in stock it can generally be sourced. Its position as one of the largest sugar beet equipment dealers in the region reflects its long-standing presence in the market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Agricultural equipment sales", "Agricultural parts distribution", "Equipment repair services", "Equipment rebuild services", "Parts sourcing and procurement"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Sugar beet farming", "Potato farming", "Hay farming", "Grain farming", "Tillage", "Planting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the largest sugar beet equipment and parts dealers in the western United States", "Shortline dealer network providing access to multiple vendors and distributors", "Full-service shop offering repair and rebuild services for agricultural machinery", "Ability to source hard-to-find parts through vendor relationships"], "facts_used": ["Established 1985 in Paul, Idaho -> db", "Largest sugar beet equipment and parts dealers in Western United States -> /", "Specializing in sugar beets, also offering equipment for potatoes, hay, tillage, grain, planting -> /", "Shortline dealer with access to many vendors and distributors -> /", "Full service shop for repair and rebuild needs -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Magic Valley Equipment is known as one of the largest sugar beet equipment and parts dealers in the Western United States.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='magic-valley-equipment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mainca USA Inc. is headquartered in St. Louis, Missouri. The company was founded in 2001 as a partnership between Dale Schmidt and Mainca Equipamentos Carnicos S.L. of Barcelona, Spain, to expand Mainca''s North American distribution of meat and food processing equipment. Dale Schmidt brought 25 years of experience from managing his family''s meat processing equipment distribution business, which had been operating since 1942.

Mainca USA imports and distributes European-made equipment for the meat and food processing industries through a network of more than 100 distributors across the United States and Canada. The product lineup includes brands such as Mainca, Jeros, Suhner, Gaser, and Lorenzo Barroso. Notable equipment includes the PQ- a hydraulic stuffer-driven double clipping system described as the first of its kind.

The company serves meat and food processors, particularly small to medium-sized operations seeking speed, accuracy, and portioning capabilities. Its distributor network reaches processors throughout North America, providing equipment for production lines that require reliable clipping, stuffing, and processing machinery.

The venture was built on the combination of Dale Schmidt''s deep industry knowledge and Mainca''s European manufacturing expertise. Mainca USA emphasizes quality, value, and dependability, positioning itself as a source for durable, reliable equipment and unique systems like the hydraulic stuffer-driven double clipper that are not available elsewhere.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Distribution of European meat processing equipment", "Importation of food processing machinery", "Dealer network management across U.S. and Canada", "Technical support for meat processing equipment"], "industries": ["Meat processing", "Food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Double Clipper with Hydraulic Stuffer", "PQ-360 Clipper Drive", "Mainca equipment", "Jeros equipment", "Suhner equipment", "Gaser equipment", "Lorenzo Barroso equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 as partnership between Dale Schmidt and Mainca Equipamentos Carnicos S.L. -> /", "Headquarters in St. Louis, Missouri -> /", "Over 100 distributors across U.S. and Canada -> /", "Brands: Mainca, Jeros, Suhner, Gaser, Lorenzo Barroso -> /", "PQ-360 Clipper Drive hydraulic stuffer-driven double clipper -> /", "Schmidt family company founded 1942 -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Mainca USA provides a wide range of European made equipment for the meat and food processing industries right here in North America.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mainca-usa-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Commercial Solar was founded in 2020 by Jason Stutheit in Hermon, Maine. Stutheit started the company after identifying a gap between what solar contractors offered and the actual needs of the industry. The business operates from Hermon and serves customers across the state.

The company provides full-service solar solutions including system design, installation, and ongoing maintenance. It also sells solar components such as inverters, light fixtures, panels, and ground-mount helical piles, and offers packaged DIY kits for self-installation. In addition, Maine Commercial Solar rents land for community solar farms in Central Maine Power and Versant (Emera) utility territories, allowing customers to host systems off-site.

Its customer base spans construction firms, commercial property owners, and residential homeowners. The firm works with major panel brands including REC, Canadian Solar, LG, Solaria, and Q-CELLS, and advertises panel pricing starting at $0.53 per watt.

The company emphasizes direct communication and aims to be the sole supplier and installer for its clients, highlighting quick turnaround and personalized support as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Solar installation", "Solar system service", "Solar component sales", "DIY solar package sales", "Community solar farm land rental", "Helical pile installation"], "industries": ["Construction", "Commercial", "Residential", "Community solar"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Panels priced from $0.53 per watt", "Community solar land rental in CMP and Versant territories", "DIY solar package sales", "Full design, installation, and service", "Carries major brands: REC, Canadian Solar, LG, Solaria, Q-CELLS"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020 by Jason Stutheit -> db", "Headquarters Hermon, Maine -> db", "Offers solar design, installation, service, component sales, DIY packages -> /", "Community solar farm land rental in CMP and Versant territories -> /", "Serves construction businesses, commercial customers, homeowners -> /", "Carries brands REC, Canadian Solar, LG, Solaria, Q-CELLS -> /", "Panel pricing starting at $0.53 per watt -> /", "Founder noticed gap between industry needs and contractor offerings -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We offer full design, installation and service of new systems, component sales and service and also package sales for the do-it yourself.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-commercial-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Energy Experts is based in Buxton, Maine, and was founded in 2021 by Samuel Legere, Cameron Kerr‑Cavanagh, and Corey Levy. The company traces its start to Legere knocking on doors during a Maine winter, aiming to give homeowners an alternative to rising utility rates controlled by a foreign‑owned power monopoly.

The firm installs solar photovoltaic systems, high‑efficiency heat pumps, and roofing for residential and commercial customers across southern Maine.

Customers are primarily Maine homeowners and businesses seeking to lower energy costs and gain independence from Central Maine Power. The company cites examples of homeowners who have cut heating and cooling expenses by pairing solar with heat pumps, achieving a combined payback as short as 2.5 years.

Legere and his partners say they started the business to make the switch to solar simple, transparent, and enjoyable — emphasizing honest communication, industry‑warranties, and a goal of helping 10,000 Maine families become power independent.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system installation", "Heat pump installation", "Roofing installation and replacement", "Solar panel maintenance and service", "Energy analysis and efficiency consultation", "Solar system design and permitting", "Financing and incentive assistance"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Renewable energy", "Energy efficiency", "Home improvement"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Heat pumps", "Roofing materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1-3 days for solar panel installation; same day for heat pump installation", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["4.5-year average ROI on solar panel systems", "$0 down bill-swap program (fixed $200/month solar bill)", "Same-day heat pump installation", "Industry-leading warranties on all installations", "Transparent pricing with free estimates"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2021 -> db", "Headquarters Buxton, Maine -> db", "Founder Sam Legere -> /about-us", "Co-owners Cameron Kerr-Cavanagh, Corey Levy -> /about-us", "Services: solar, heat pump, roofing installation -> /services", "Bill-swap program ($250 to $200 fixed) -> /, /about-us", "ROI claims: 4.5 years solar, 6.5 years heat pump, 2.5 years combined -> /, /about-us", "Installation timeline: 1-3 days solar, same day heat pump -> /services", "Team members listed (installers, project management, marketing) -> /about-us", "Coverage area: southern Maine -> /, /about-us", "Mission: help 10,000 Maine homeowners become power independent -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Maine Energy Experts installs high-quality solar panels and heat pumps in Maine", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/maine-energy-experts/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-energy-experts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Technology Group was founded in 2012 in Oakland, Maine, with a mission to deliver reliable, no-nonsense IT services to businesses across the state. The company was started out of frustration with providers that overcomplicated technology and pushed unnecessary solutions, choosing instead to focus on fast response times, clear communication, and practical, business-driven IT support.

Its offerings include proactive monitoring and maintenance, cybersecurity measures, strategic IT planning, and consultation, all backed by a guaranteed one-hour emergency response time and a 100% satisfaction guarantee. The company emphasizes eliminating technical jargon and tailoring solutions to actual business needs rather than selling add-ons.

Current clients include law firms such as Bloomer-Russell-Beaupain, financial groups like Thompson Financial Group, and nonprofits such as Becket Maine, which relies on the company for secure, compliant systems that support care delivery.

The company was founded to address a gap in the market where IT providers prioritized sales over service, to overcomplicated systems and bloated contracts. Its stated differentiators are rapid response, honest communication, proactive problem prevention, and long-term partnerships built on trust, with the goal of making IT reliable enough that clients rarely have to think about it.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Managed IT Services", "VoIP Solutions", "Nonprofit IT Services", "Fleet IT Services", "IT Consultation", "Cybersecurity", "Proactive Monitoring and Maintenance", "Strategic IT Planning", "Emergency IT Support", "IT Security and Compliance"], "industries": ["Legal Services", "Financial Services", "Nonprofit Organizations", "Healthcare and Social Services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Guaranteed one-hour emergency response time", "100% satisfaction guarantee on all IT services", "Clear communication without technical jargon", "Proactive IT support to prevent issues before they happen", "Tailored, business-driven solutions with no unnecessary add-ons"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Oakland, Maine -> db", "CEO Jonathan Perkins -> /", "One-hour emergency response guarantee -> /about-us", "100% satisfaction guarantee -> /about-us", "Services: Managed IT, VoIP, Nonprofit IT, Fleet IT -> /", "Clients: Bloomer-Russell-Beaupain, Thompson Financial Group, Becket Maine -> /", "Values: Knowledge, Relationships, Teamwork, Trust, Passion for Service -> /about-us", "Mission and vision statements -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We Provide Reliable IT Services and Solutions for Maine Businesses.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/maine-technology-group/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-technology-group' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mammoth Manufacturing operates from Eugene, Oregon, where it was established in 1996 by owner Ken Rodgers. Rodgers began producing sewn goods in 1984, crafting rafting D-rings in his garage after failing to find suitable options on the market. That venture evolved into Mammoth Manufacturing and its sister brand Whitewater Designs, growing to a team of up to 10 employees.

The shop provides contract sewing and production services, specializing in techniques such as industrial sewing (single- and double-needle), bar tacking, pattern tacking, five-thread surging, die cutting, hot-knife cutting, kick-press grommet and hole punching, and high-frequency RF welding. A climate-controlled, pest-free warehouse supports material storage and logistics, allowing the company to ship anything from single units to 1,000-unit runs.

The company focuses on the outdoor industry, working with materials including Cordura, vinyl, webbing, nylon fabric, mesh, rope, and Hypalon. It also stocks hardware such as buckles, toggles, zippers, hook-and-loop fasteners, cams, and grommets, and can source additional components as needed. Customers range from small-scale custom orders to larger manufacturing programs.

Mammoth Manufacturing emphasizes its 30-plus years of experience, versatile capabilities, rigorous quality control, and a customer-oriented approach as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial sewing (single-needle, double-needle)", "Bar tacking", "Pattern tacking", "Five-thread surging", "Die cutting", "Hot knife cutting", "RF welding (high frequency)", "Grommet and hole punching (kickpress)", "Die pressing", "Design and quality control"], "industries": ["Outdoor industry"], "materials": ["Cordura", "Vinyl", "Webbing", "Nylon fabric", "Rope", "Mesh", "Hypalon", "Buckles", "Toggles", "Zippers", "Hook-and-loop fasteners", "Cams", "Grommets"], "equipment": ["Double Needle Industrial Sewing Machines", "Single Needle Industrial Sewing Machines", "Bar Tack Machines", "Pattern Tack Machines", "5 Thread Surgers", "Hot Knife", "Die Presses", "Kickpress Grommet/Hole Punch", "High Frequency RF Welding Machine"], "volume": "1 to 1,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30+ years of experience in sewn goods manufacturing", "Versatile capabilities across sewing, welding, and cutting processes", "Rigorous quality control measures on every product", "Customer-oriented approach with design consultation support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Employee count 10 -> db and / (About us)", "Headquarters Eugene, Oregon -> db and /", "Owner Ken Rodgers started in 1984 making D-rings in garage -> / (About us)", "Specializations: sewing, die cutting, RF welding, hot knife, bar tacking -> / (Unmatched Specializations)", "Materials: Cordura, vinyl, webbing, nylon, mesh, rope, Hypalon -> / and /capabilities", "Hardware: buckles, toggles, zippers, hook/loop, cams, grommets -> /capabilities", "Equipment list -> /capabilities", "Warehouse: climate-controlled, pest-free, skid storage -> /capabilities", "Shipping 1 to 1000 units -> /capabilities", "Industries: outdoor industry -> / (Unmatched Specializations)", "Differentiators: 30+ years experience, versatile capabilities, quality assurance, customer-oriented -> / (Why Choose Mammoth Manufacturing)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Sewing and Production in Eugene Oregon", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mammoth-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Manufacture Good, originally founded as Magic City Woodworks in 2013, operates from a training campus in downtown Birmingham, Alabama. The organization began in a borrowed one-car garage in nearby Hoover when founder Lawrence Sheffield launched a grassroots effort to teach woodworking trades to young men alongside spiritual mentorship. The Lawson family provided the initial workspace, and within a year the program outgrew the space, eventually receiving a donated commercial warehouse from the Cathey family that enabled expansion into a dedicated facility.

A master craftsman team oversees production, which also includes a firewood operation that cuts, splits, seasons, delivers, and stacks wood for customers. The apprenticeship program pays participants while they learn woodworking and life skills, with the workshop serving as both a production floor and a training ground.

Finished pieces are sold to residential clients, churches, and businesses nationwide, while the firewood service delivers directly to local customers. The apprentice cohort—typically young men seeking trade skills and personal development—forms the core labor force, supported by mentors, shop staff, and an executive team that includes an executive director, operations director, and apprenticeship foreman. A board of directors drawn from local construction, finance, and healthcare sectors provides governance.

Sheffield has stated that the enterprise was started to create a workshop where young men could come to faith while developing the hands and minds needed to provide for themselves and their families. The organization describes its model as “making disciples while making good things,” using product revenue and donor support to sustain a ministry that aims to prepare participants for roles as husbands, fathers, craftsmen, and community leaders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and manufacturing", "Cabinetmaking / millwork", "Woodworking apprenticeship training", "Firewood processing (cutting, splitting, seasoning)", "Firewood delivery and stacking"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Woodworking", "Workforce development", "Nonprofit / social enterprise", "Firewood supply"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Apprenticeship model that pays participants to learn woodworking and life skills while producing sellable goods", "Handcrafted custom furniture built in a Birmingham woodshop by trainees under master craftsman supervision", "Firewood service that cuts, splits, seasons, delivers, and stacks orders on-site", "Nonprofit ministry structure funded through product sales and charitable donations", "Training campus in downtown Birmingham developed from a donated warehouse"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 as Magic City Woodworks -> /about", "Founder Lawrence Sheffield -> /about", "Started in Lawson family garage in Hoover, Alabama -> /about", "Received donated warehouse from Cathey family -> /about", "Now operates training campus in downtown Birmingham -> /about", "Produces handcrafted tables, desks, seating, shelves, custom cabinetry -> /, /about", "Firewood cutting, splitting, drying, delivery, stacking -> /", "Apprenticeship program pays young men to learn woodworking and life skills -> /, /about", "Products sold to homes, churches, businesses nationwide -> /about", "Team includes executive director, shop staff, apprenticeship foreman, master craftsmen, operations director -> /about", "Board of directors includes construction, finance, healthcare leaders -> /about", "Mission: workforce development with spiritual growth -> /, /about", "Headquarters Birmingham, Alabama -> db, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "apprentices support the production of custom furniture which is designed and made right here in our local Birmingham woodshop", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='manufacture-good' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Manufacturing Solutions, Inc. (MSI) was founded in 1996 by Garret Hirchak in Morrisville, Vermont. Hirchak serves as CEO, and Bethany Salvas has been president since the company''s inception. The business began as a contract manufacturing operation focused on bringing product ideas to reality through fabrication, assembly, and finishing services.

Today MSI operates a vertically integrated facility in Morrisville offering CNC machining (milling and turning), sheet metal fabrication, welding, automated powder coating on a Gema SMART Series line, 3D printing, and both electrical and mechanical assembly. The company also provides fulfillment services including picking, kitting, packing, warehousing, and third‑party logistics, allowing it to manage projects from prototype through high‑volume production and delivery.

MSI serves original equipment manufacturers and other businesses requiring precision metal parts, coated finishes, and full supply‑chain support. Its NAICS codes span machine shops, sheet metal work, fabricated metal products, and warehousing, though the company does not publicly list specific industry verticals or named customers.

The company emphasizes a vertically integrated model—keeping equipment, team, and processes under one roof—to improve communication, speed, and quality control. Founder Garret Hirchak has stated that the goal is to “competitively manufacture products in the USA,” and the leadership team cites values such as accountability, flexibility, and collaboration as cultural differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Welding", "Powder coating (automated, Gema SMART Series)", "3D printing", "Electrical assembly", "Mechanical assembly", "Metal stamping", "Waterjet cutting", "Custom die cutting", "Sheet cutting", "Metal forming and bending", "Precision cutting", "Surface grinding", "Precision grinding", "Specialty fabric/material cutting", "Picking, kitting, and packing", "Warehousing and distribution", "Inventory storage", "Supply chain management", "Third-party logistics (3PL)", "Design, engineering, and prototyping", "Project management"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless Steel"], "equipment": ["Gema SMART Series automated powder coating line"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated facility with all equipment, team, and processes under one roof", "ISO 9001:2015 and ITAR certified quality system", "Automated powder coating line (Gema SMART Series) for consistent, low\u2011waste finishes", "End\u2011to\u2011end contract manufacturing from prototyping through fulfillment and global logistics", "3PL and supply\u2011chain management services including kitting, warehousing, and worldwide shipping"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 by Garret Hirchak -> /about", "Headquarters Morrisville, VT -> /about", "CEO Garret Hirchak, President Bethany Salvas -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 and ITAR certifications -> /services", "CAGE code 7SU9 -> /services", "Vertically integrated model -> /services", "Automated powder coating line Gema SMART Series -> db", "Services: CNC machining, sheet metal fabrication, welding, 3D printing, assembly, fulfillment, logistics -> /services, /", "Materials: aluminum, stainless steel -> /", "Volume: prototype to high-volume production -> /, /services", "Company values (accountability, flexibility, collaboration, etc.) -> /about", "NAICS codes -> /services", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a leading contract manufacturer, MSI offers end-to-end solutions, from prototyping and production to logistics and fulfillment.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "7SU9", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/manufacturing-solutions-inc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='manufacturing-solutions-inc-msi' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Marchel Industries was founded in 1992 in Spartanburg, South Carolina, as an American-based precision injection molding and manufacturing company. In February 2023 the business was acquired by Plastifab, a extrusion firm, to create a complete plastics partner offering both extrusion and injection molding services.

The company operates a 35,000-square-foot climate-controlled facility equipped with 20- to 400-ton injection molding presses, CNC machining centers, and EDM equipment. Its capabilities span plastic injection molding, precision machining, EDM machining, plastic design, custom molding, reverse engineering, prototyping, parts assembly, testing, and dimensional analysis. The firm also provides project management from design through manufacturing and delivery.

Marchel serves OEMs, medical, government, military, industrial, and telecommunications sectors. It handles both high-volume OEM production and short-run concept modeling projects.

The company emphasizes Lean Manufacturing principles, ISO 9001:2015 certification, in-house design and machining, and a goal of zero defects. It aims to be the "Plastic Injection Molded Part Vendor of Choice" through Southern hospitality, high-quality manufacturing, and state-of-the-art technology.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding (20-400 ton)", "Precision machining", "EDM machining", "Plastic design", "Custom molding", "Reverse engineering", "Prototyping", "Parts assembly", "Testing", "Dimensional analysis", "Project management", "Short run plastic injection molding", "Extrusion"], "industries": ["OEM", "Medical", "Government", "Military", "Industrial", "Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["20-400 ton injection molding presses", "CNC machining centers", "EDM machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lean Manufacturing principles", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "In-house machining, molding, design & engineering, and quality departments", "State-of-the-art injection molding technologies and process control systems", "Complete supply chain management from design through manufacturing and delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992 in Spartanburg, South Carolina -> /about-us", "Acquired by Plastifab in February 2023 -> /about-us", "35,000 square foot climate controlled facility -> /", "20-400 ton press injection molding -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> / and /about-us", "Capabilities: precision machining, EDM machining, plastic design, custom molding, reverse engineering, prototyping, parts assembly, testing, dimensional analysis -> /", "Industries served: OEM, medical, government, military, industrial -> /", "Telecommunications industry -> db (industries_served)", "Lean Manufacturing principles -> /about-us", "In-house machining, molding, design & engineering, quality departments -> /about-us", "Proprietary materials selection software -> /", "Headquarters: 100 South West Dr., Spartanburg, SC 29303 -> / and /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db (linkedin_url)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1992 in Spartanburg, South Carolina, Marchel Industries is an American-based precision injection molding and manufacturing company providing the highest quality and service to our customer base.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/marchel-industries/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='marchel-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company maintains a 10,000-square-foot showroom on Gleneagles Court that displays one of the largest office furniture selections in the state.

The business sells new, remanufactured, and used office furniture across categories including cubicles, desks, seating, filing and storage, tables, and accessories. It partners with multiple manufacturers — among them Steelcase and N9NE Furniture Group — to stock a range of price points. In addition to product sales, Mark Downs provides complimentary space planning and design services, using 3D rendering software to develop floor plans and furniture recommendations for projects of any size.

Customers span corporate offices, call centers, healthcare practices, and home offices throughout the Baltimore–Washington corridor. Reviews cite engagements ranging from a 25-year call-center buyer outfitting a large center to a small therapy suite needing only a few pieces. The company also serves residential buyers seeking single items such as ergonomic chairs.

