ounded 2001 -> db", "Headquarters Atlanta, GA -> db", "CEO Gary Woodall founded company after 30 years commercial roofing experience -> /", "President Michael Marchman background in automotive sales -> /", "Standard roofing orders completed within 24-48 hours -> /", "ES-1 Certified and fabricated to SMACNA Standards -> /", "Press-brake capabilities up to 12'' lengths for steel and aluminum -> /", "In-house welding and painting available for mill finish steel and aluminum -> /", "Own delivery fleet to cut down project delays -> /capabilities", "Stock variety of industry standard aluminum, steel & stainless -> /capabilities", "Industries: commercial roofing, architectural, curtain wall, store front -> /", "Government/military contract sales experience (Sean Rhodes) -> /", "Materials: Kynar coated, galvanized, Galvalume, anodized, mill finish, stainless -> /", "Team members: Justin Schneider, Teagan Rhodes, Doug Gallaway, Gary Woodall, Michael Marchman, Sean Rhodes -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a fast-paced, specialized custom sheet metal fabrication shop for Commercial Roofing and Architectural Projects.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metalpride-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metro Assemblies, Inc. was founded in 1971 by Robert and Priscilla Barnick in a family garage in Minneapolis, Minnesota. The family-owned business has grown into a multi-million-dollar contract manufacturer while remaining headquartered in Minneapolis.

The company produces custom wire and cable assemblies, including wire harnesses, cable assemblies, insert overmolded cables, box builds, and electro-mechanical assemblies. Its capabilities span automatic wire cutting and stripping, terminal crimping, soldering, ultrasonic splicing and welding, sleeving, heat shrink, potting, CNC and laser cutting, and 3D printing. Metro supports programs from rapid prototyping through low-volume specialty runs to higher-volume steady-state production.

Metro serves OEMs and contract manufacturers across medical device, industrial automation, defense, consumer electronics, agriculture, telecommunications, and automotive sectors. Its customer base ranges from start-ups to Fortune 50 corporations.

The company emphasizes its founding values of high-quality products and excellent customer service, backed by ISO 9001 certification, UL listing (ZPFW2/8), and adherence to IPC/WHMA-A-620 workmanship standards. Metro highlights on-time delivery, competitive pricing, and a team of qualified experts as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','UL Listed (ZPFW2/8)','IPC/WHMA-A-620']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assemblies", "Wire harnesses", "Insert overmolding", "Box build / electro-mechanical assemblies", "Prototyping", "Automatic wire cutting & stripping", "Terminal crimping", "Soldering of components", "Ultrasonic splicing", "Ultrasonic welding", "Sleeving & heat shrink", "Potting / epoxy / waterproofing", "CNC & laser cutting", "3D printing", "Electrical & mechanical testing", "Quality assurance processing"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Industrial automation", "Defense", "Consumer electronics", "Agriculture", "Telecommunications", "Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automatic wire cutting & wire stripping", "Insert overmolding of cable", "Ultrasonic splicing", "Terminal crimping", "Soldering of components", "Sleeving & heat shrink", "Ultrasonic welding", "Electrical & mechanical testing", "Potting / epoxy / waterproofing", "CNC & laser cutting", "3D printing"], "volume": "Prototype through full production, including low-volume specialty builds and higher-volume steady-state programs", "lead_time": "Lead times vary by complexity and volume; contact for project-specific estimate", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001 certified and UL listed (ZPFW2/8)", "Manufactures to IPC/WHMA-A-620 standards", "Prototype through full production support", "Insert overmolding and custom molded cable assemblies", "On-time delivery commitment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 by Robert and Priscilla Barnick -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Family-owned, started in family garage -> /about-us", 