UPDATE companies SET description='Michigan Precision Fabricators, LLC was founded in 2008 in Commerce Township, Michigan. The company was established by a group of founders who identified a gap in the supply chain for industrial-grade dampers and expansion joints, aiming to deliver dependable, high-quality products quickly and at competitive cost.

The company manufactures a range of dampers — including butterfly, louver, diverter, barometric, radial vane, and paddle types — as well as expansion joints. It operates a fully integrated CNC machine shop where skilled machinists design and produce all bracketry and drive components to ISO 5211 standards, and also offers automation packages, project management, spare-parts inventory services, and field maintenance, inspection, commissioning, and repair. The team brings more than 20 years of industry experience and 40 years in metal fabrication.

Its products serve steel processing plants, municipalities, industrial wastewater treatment facilities, chemical and petrochemical complexes, and tier-one automotive plants, among other industrial sectors.

The founders started the business to address a market shortage of rapidly produced, reliable damper and expansion-joint solutions. The company’s stated mission is to develop partnerships by providing superior products at low cost with on-time delivery, guided by a vision of harnessing collective genius and embracing change.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Damper manufacturing", "Expansion joint manufacturing", "CNC machining", "Automation package integration", "Project management", "Spare parts inventory management", "Field service and maintenance", "Design and fabrication of bracketry and drive components", "ISO 5211 compliant mounting", "Custom damper design", "Remote linkage kits"], "industries": ["Steel processing", "Municipalities", "Industrial wastewater treatment", "Chemical and petrochemical", "Tier-one automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Rapid production of dampers and expansion joints without compromising quality", "Fully integrated CNC machine shop for custom bracketry and drive components", "Certified technicians available for field inspections, commissioning, and repair", "Project management with dedicated 2\u20135 person teams for transparency", "Spare-parts inventory management and stocking at company facilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 in Commerce Township, Michigan -> db, /about", "Manufactures butterfly, louver, diverter, barometric, radial vane, paddle dampers and expansion joints -> /, /about", "Operates fully integrated CNC machine shop for bracketry and drive components -> /services", "Offers automation packages, project management, spare parts inventory, field maintenance -> /services", "Team has 20+ years industry experience and 40 years metal fabrication -> /", "Serves steel processing, municipalities, wastewater treatment, chemical/petrochemical, tier-one automotive -> /about", "Mission: develop partnerships with superior products at low cost, on-time delivery -> /about", "Vision: harness collective genius, embrace change -> /about", "ISO 5211 standards followed for mounting -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MPF and its members are pioneers in the manufacturing of Industrial Grade Dampers and Expansion Joints", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='michigan-precision-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Micro Control Company was founded in 1972 in Arden Hills, Minnesota. The company began as a pioneer in the test and measurement segment of the electronics industry, developing the industry''s first microprocessor-controlled test system.

Today, the company designs and manufactures high-performance burn-in with test systems, custom burn-in boards, and supporting accessories for semiconductor manufacturers. Its 157,000-square-foot facility houses in-house system assembly, integration, and validation, supported by a workforce in which one-third are engineers. The product line spans standard burn-in applications to systems capable of stressing devices at 2,000+ watts per device under test with individual temperature control. Automation integration—including automated loading, mobile robotics, and the proprietary C-Breez software platform—extends across the portfolio.

Micro Control serves the world''s semiconductor manufacturers across AI and high-performance computing, automotive, aerospace, defense, advanced manufacturing, consumer electronics, and custom silicon markets. Its systems are used for production screening, qualification, and reliability testing of high-pin-count and high-power devices.

The company emphasizes an engineering-first culture, with design, applications, manufacturing, and service teams working as a single unit from concept through deployment. It highlights a 50-plus-year history of technical breakthroughs, a global support network spanning 15 countries, and a commitment to supporting installed systems for seven or more years with critical spare parts on standby.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Burn-in with test systems design and manufacturing", "Custom burn-in board design and manufacturing", "Burn-in accessories manufacturing", "High-power burn-in test (2000+ W DUTs)", "Individual temperature control (ITC) burn-in", "Automation integration (automated loading, mobile robotics, cross-platform software)", "C-Breez software platform development and updates", "Engineering & R&D collaboration", "In-house system assembly, integration, and validation", "Field services (installation, troubleshooting, training)", "Upgrade & modernization services for installed systems", "Compliance & qualification support", "Burn-in efficiency & facility optimization", "Lifecycle management & spare parts support", "Global service & support across 15 countries", "High pin count device testing", "Parallel device testing", "Logic/memory burn-in test applications", "Production burn-in", "Signal integrity and thermal stability design"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "AI / high-performance computing", "Automotive", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Advanced manufacturing", "Consumer electronics", "Custom silicon"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["C-Breez software platform", "Automated loading systems", "Mobile robotics", "Burn-in with test systems", "Burn-in boards"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["50+ years of burn-in expertise since 1972", "Engineering-first culture with 33% of staff as engineers", "In-house manufacturing in 157,000 sq. ft. facility", "Global support across 15 countries with dedicated representatives", "C-Breez software platform with 12 updates per year"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Arden Hills, Minnesota -> db", "157,000 sq. ft. facility -> /services", "33% of staff are engineers -> /services", "15 countries with dedicated representatives -> /services", "14 person dedicated field service team -> /services", "12 software updates per year -> /services", "25 years continuous development -> /services", "7+ years active support after purchase -> /services", "100% systems have critical spare parts on standby -> /services", "100% projects involve customer collaboration -> /services", "100% future systems designed with customer collaboration -> /services", "100% systems run on C-Breez -> /services", "High-power burn-in up to 2000+ W DUTs -> /", "Individual temperature control (ITC) burn-in -> /", "Automation integration (automated loading, mobile robotics) -> /about-us", "C-Breez software platform -> /services", "Industries served: AI, automotive, aerospace, defense, advanced manufacturing, consumer electronics, custom silicon -> /about-us", "Engineering-first culture, one team from design to deployment -> /about-us", "Global leader in burn-in with test systems -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Micro Control Company designs and manufactures high-performance burn-in with test systems, boards, and integrated solutions for the world''s leading semiconductor manufacturers.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='micro-control-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MicroTek, a non-profit manufacturer, was founded in 1983 in Chicopee Falls, Massachusetts. The organization began in a century-old mill building with a mission to connect people as well as electronic parts, specifically providing employment support for individuals with developmental and intellectual disabilities in a self-sustaining, community-based manufacturing setting.

The company designs and produces custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, control panels, and complete electro-mechanical assemblies. Its 55,000-square-foot facility in Chicopee houses engineering and design services using SolidWorks, Visio, and AutoCAD, along with prototyping, automated tooling, and material management programs such as VMI and Kanban. Production relies on Komax cut/strip/crimp machines, automated stripping equipment, hot-stamp wire marking, and automated label-wrapping systems, all adhering to IPC standards for crimp height and pull testing.

MicroTek serves the medical, scientific, and security industries worldwide, shipping to multiple international addresses. The firm maintains associations with IPC/WHMA, the Social Enterprise Alliance, the Association for Developmental Disabilities Providers, and Associated Industries of Massachusetts.

As a social enterprise, MicroTek differentiates itself by integrating a diverse workforce—including employees with disabilities—into high-quality manufacturing. The organization emphasizes a human approach to production, combining rigorous quality systems with a mission-driven culture that prioritizes employee safety and continuous training.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assemblies", "Wire harnesses", "Control systems & panels", "Electro-mechanical assemblies", "Engineering & design (SolidWorks, Visio, AutoCAD)", "Prototyping", "Tooling & automation", "Material management (VMI, Kanban, kitting, just-in-time fulfillment)", "Shipping (worldwide, multi-address)", "Automated wire cutting, stripping, crimping (Komax)", "Wire marking (hot stamp)", "Automated self-laminating label wrapping", "IPC standards compliance (crimp height, pull test)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Scientific", "Security"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Komax cut/strip/crimp equipment", "Automated stripping equipment", "Hot stamp equipment", "Automated self-laminating label wrapping equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Non-profit social enterprise employing individuals with developmental and intellectual disabilities", "IPC/WHMA standards compliance for crimp height and pull testing", "Automated Komax cut/strip/crimp equipment for repeatable wire processing", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) and Kanban material management programs", "Worldwide shipping with multi-address logistics management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 in Chicopee Falls, MA -> /about-us", "Non-profit mission to employ individuals with disabilities -> /about-us", "Facility history: 24,000 sq ft (2003), 55,000 sq ft (2014) -> /about-us", "Custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, control panels, electro-mechanical assemblies -> /", "Engineering & design with SolidWorks, Visio, AutoCAD -> /services", "Prototyping, tooling & automation, material management (VMI, Kanban), shipping -> /services", "Komax cut/strip/crimp equipment, automated stripping, hot stamp, automated label wrapping -> /services", "IPC standards for crimp height and pull test -> /services", "Industries served: medical, scientific, security -> /", "Associations: IPC/WHMA, SEA, ADDP, AIM -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Chicopee, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded year: 1983 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MicroTek provides custom cable and wire configurations for equipment used in the medical, scientific and security industries around the world.", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='microtek-cables' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mid-Atlantic Plastics was founded in 2005 in Rosedale, Maryland, driven by customer demand for quality plastic fabrication. The company began with a focus on delivering reliable fabrication services across diverse industries.

The shop specializes in custom plastic fabrication, offering CNC routing, machining, edge finishing, welding, engraving, line bending, and drilling. With four CNC routers—including a large-format machine handling sheets up to 80 by 121 inches—a HendrickSaw panel saw capable of 126 by 120 inches, and a strip heater rig that can bend up to four 48-inch-wide pieces simultaneously, the facility runs jobs from single prototypes to large production runs.

Customers span health care, law enforcement, food processing, military, machine shops, and residential projects. Long-term clients include a sign company relying on custom acrylic signage and a partner of 15 years using routing, tapping, bending, machining, polishing, and gluing services.

